      "chunk_index": 1,
      "text": "### 2. Attendance and Condonation Regulations\n\n2.1. Minimum Attendance Requirement:\n\nEvery registered student must secure a minimum of 75% aggregate attendance in all registered theory and laboratory courses in a semester to be permitted to sit for the Semester End Examinations (SEE).\n\n2.2. Attendance Condonation on Medical Grounds:\n\nThe Dean of Academic Affairs may condone shortage of attendance up to 10% (i.e., attendance between 65% and 74.9%) on genuine medical grounds or authorized participation in university-level sports/cultural events, provided:\n\n- The student submits an authentic medical certificate and hospital discharge summary within three days of resuming classes.\n\n- The student pays the prescribed non-refundable attendance condonation fee.\n\n2.3. Detention:\n\nStudents securing aggregate attendance below 65% in a semester are not eligible for condonation under any circumstances. Such students shall be detained and must repeat the semester in subsequent academic years.",
