      "chunk_index": 2,
      "text": "### 3. Examination and Evaluation Scheme\n\n3.1. Course Weightage:\n\nThe performance of a student in each semester course is evaluated for a maximum of 100 marks:\n\n- Continuous Internal Evaluation (CIE): 40 Marks.\n\n- Semester End Examination (SEE): 60 Marks.\n\n3.2. Continuous Internal Evaluation (CIE) Breakdown:\n\n- Mid-Semester Examination I: 15 Marks (conducted at end of first spell).\n\n- Mid-Semester Examination II: 15 Marks (conducted at end of second spell).\n\n- Continuous Assignments / Quizzes / Tutorial Tests: 10 Marks.\n\nThe final Mid-Semester Examination score is computed as the average or weighted combination of both examinations according to departmental norms.\n\n3.3. Minimum Passing Criteria:\n\nA student is declared passed in a course if they secure:\n\n- A minimum of 40% (24 marks out of 60) in the Semester End Examination (SEE).\n\n- An aggregate of at least 40% (40 marks out of 100) combining CIE and SEE.",
