    {
      "chunk_id": "5e0976ef08031bc724d13dd498b9011401ea917213646b351c0d87b718658ad6_chunk_0003",
      "document_id": "5e0976ef08031bc724d13dd498b9011401ea917213646b351c0d87b718658ad6",
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "text": "### 4. Grading System and CGPA Calculation\n\n4.1. Ten-Point Grading Scale:\n\nAcademic performance is awarded on a 10-point letter grading scale:\n\n- O (Outstanding): 90% to 100% | Grade Point: 10\n\n- A+ (Excellent): 80% to 89% | Grade Point: 9\n\n- A (Very Good): 70% to 79% | Grade Point: 8\n\n- B+ (Good): 60% to 69% | Grade Point: 7\n\n- B (Above Average): 50% to 59% | Grade Point: 6\n\n- C (Average): 45% to 49% | Grade Point: 5\n\n- P (Pass): 40% to 44% | Grade Point: 4\n\n- F (Fail): Below 40% | Grade Point: 0\n\n- Ab (Absent): Did not appear | Grade Point: 0\n\n4.2. Grade Point Average Calculations:\n\nSemester Grade Point Average (SGPA) is calculated as:\n\nSGPA = Sum(Course_Credits * Grade_Points) / Sum(Course_Credits) for that semester.\n\nCumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) is calculated across all completed semesters:\n\nCGPA = Sum(All_Course_Credits * Grade_Points) / Sum(All_Course_Credits).\n\n4.3. Award of Degree Classification:\n\n- First Class with Distinction: CGPA >= 8.0 with no backlogs in first attempt.\n\n- First Class: CGPA >= 6.5 and < 8.0.\n\n- Second Class: CGPA >= 5.5 and < 6.5.\n\n- Pass Division: CGPA >= 5.0 and < 5.5.\n\nMinimum CGPA required for degree award is 5.0.",
